= Reproducible computational research — Technical =

A computational result can be modeled as R=F(D,C,P,E), where D is identified input data, C code/workflow version, P parameters/seeds and E execution environment/dependencies. Reproducibility requires enough provenance to reconstruct these inputs and transformations, plus a declared criterion for what counts as the same result.

== Modeling / evidence cautions ==
* reproducible computational research ≠ general reproducibility by identity
* reproducibility ≠ replication
* open code alone ≠ reproducible workflow

